BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noisy Futures - 10 Year Anniversary Party
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260419T150000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260419T210000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001255-1776610800-1776632400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-08-at-3.40.39-pm.png
CREATED:20260408T054302Z
DESCRIPTION:Noisy Futures is turning 10 – and we’re throwing a party t
 o celebrate! \n\n\n\nJoin us on Sunday 19 April at Gang Gang Café & Bar f
 or a special anniversary event marking a decade of Noisy Futures. \n\n\n\n
 For ten years\, we’ve been creating safe and inclusive spaces where youn
 g people can learn\, create and collaborate through music. This celebratio
 n brings together the community that has grown alongside us: the young peo
 ple\, artists\, mentors and scene who have made Noisy Futures what it is t
 oday. \n\n\n\nCome along for an afternoon of live music from local favour
 ites and rising stars\, alongside market stalls hosted by our community 
 partners. There’ll also be hands-on creative activities throughout the d
 ay\, including including zine workshops and badge-making\, as well as o
 pportunities to learn about ways you can get involved in your local music 
 scene. \n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n\n\n\nThis is an all-
 ages\, fully accessible event. Quiet spaces will be available\, and the No
 isy Futures team will be there to help make sure everyone feels welcome an
 d supported throughout the day. \n\n\n\nIf the ticket cost is a barrier to
  attending\, please reach out to us at noisyfutures@gmail.com. We’d lov
 e to help make it possible for you to join us. \n\n\n\nSouthside Bus: A s
 huttle bus will be available for people travelling from South Canberra. If
  you’d like to reserve a seat\, please indicate this when purchasing you
 r ticket or get in touch with us via email. \n\n\n\nA huge thank you to A
 rtsACT for their generous support of this event\, and to our partners Ai
 nslie Arts Centre\, Megalo Print Studio\, and YWCA Canberra. \n\n\n\nThis 
 event is taking place on the unceded lands of the Ngunnawal & Ngambri peop
 les. This always was and always will be Aboriginal land.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T054303Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/noisy-futures-10-year-anniversary-pa
 rty/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gang Gang Comedy - Annie Boyle
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260422T193000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260422T220000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001248-1776886200-1776895200@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-25-at-12.57.11-pm.png
CREATED:20260325T015822Z
DESCRIPTION:Gang Gang Comedy brings you the best comedians from around the
  country. April is the hilarious Annie Boyle. Local supports will be the w
 onderful Anneli Cole\, funny Fateh Singh and Gang Gang Comedy favourite Su
 ma Iyer. MC for the night will be the charismatic and hilarious Cameron Ri
 bbons. \n\n\n\nAnnie Boyle is one of Australia’s most exciting rising c
 omedy voices. A RAW Comedy State Finalist and 2023 Comedy Zone performer a
 t the Melbourne International Comedy Festival\, she’s toured sold-out so
 lo shows across Australia and the UK. Trained at the National Institute of
  Dramatic Art (NIDA)\, Annie appears in Colin From Accounts (Binge) and 
 the upcoming Stan Original series The F Word. \n\n\n\n★★★★ “
 …crowds will be flocking to see her in the future for sure” — TD9  
 \n\n\n\n★★★★ “Her seemingly poker-faced presentation sprinkles 
 her show with comedic gold dust” — The Recs \n\n\n\nDoors at 7pm for a
  7:30pm show start. \n\n\n\nTix $22 online Humanitix\, $25 at the door.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T015823Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/gang-gang-comedy-annie-boyle/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:R.M.F.C Live at Gang Gang
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260425T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260425T220000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001246-1777143600-1777154400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-20-at-12.55.11-pm.png
CREATED:20260320T020027Z
DESCRIPTION:They say Canberra is our nation’s capital. R.M.F.C are visit
 ing Canberra to play their music there joined by New Age Group & Assassins
 . \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experien
 ce for all. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restro
 oms. We have zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in pl
 ace to ensure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or ass
 istance\, please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyabl
 e for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngam
 bri people\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take 
 place. We pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\,
  and recognise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and cultu
 re. We are grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T021418Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/r-m-f-c-live-at-gang-gang/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Damon Mudge & the Replacement Buses: Country Living City Benefits
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260426T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260426T210000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001249-1777226400-1777237200@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-24-at-2.28.49-pm.png
CREATED:20260325T020104Z
DESCRIPTION:Damon Mudge heads out on tour for the first time to celebrate 
 the release of his debut album\, Country Living City Benefits. Bringing hi
 s band\, the Replacement Buses\, and his unmistakable yellow piano along f
 or the ride\, Mudge delivers a punchy mix of piano-driven rock\, psychedel
 ic textures\, and sharp\, melodic songwriting. \n\n\n\nRaw\, energetic\, a
 nd a little unpredictable\, these shows mark the first chance to hear Coun
 try Living City Benefits brought to life on stage.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T020107Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/damon-mudge-the-replacement-buses-co
 untry-living-city-benefits/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LANTERNS & LINEAGES
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260502T193000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260502T223000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001256-1777750200-1777761000@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-09-at-4.18.58-pm.png
CREATED:20260409T063219Z
DESCRIPTION:LANTERNS & LINEAGES – A NIGHT OF CULTURE\, STORIES & QUEER E
 XPRESSION \n\n\n\nJoin us for an evening where artists share the stories t
 hat shaped them\, from heritage and personal history to chosen family\, id
 entity\, and the worlds that raised us. \n\n\n\nExpect: \n\n\n\n\nPole\, d
 rag\, burlesque\, cabaret\, dance\, etc.\n\n\n\nIntimate cabaret vibes\n\n
 \n\nPerformances rooted in lived experience\, culture\, and community\n\n\
 n\n\nOne night. One room. Many lineages glowing together. \n\n\n\nGA Ticke
 ts $25 online (Link in bio or Facebook Event)  \n\n\n\nDoors 6:00pm | Show
  7:30pm–10:30pm \n\n\n\nThis is an 18+ event \n\n\n\nAccessible \n\n\n\n
 Produced by Red Lanterns Haus \n\n\n\nSafe space for the LGBTQIA+ communit
 y\, SWers\, and allies \n\n\n\nWe will not tolerate homophobia\, transphob
 ia\, racism\, sexism\, ableism\, or discrimination of any kind during the 
 event
LAST-MODIFIED:20260410T110530Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/lanterns-lineages/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spellbound - Readings and Music (Lost Souls/Macabre Dreams)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260507T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260507T210000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001254-1778178600-1778187600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-08-at-3.18.45-pm.png
CREATED:20260408T052058Z
DESCRIPTION:Would you like to try living deliciously? Want to gather with 
 others venerating the gods of old? \n\n\n\nJoin us for a taste of witchy r
 eadings and music and to be spellbound at Gang Gang café on THURSDAY 07th
  MAY 2026. And help us celebrate the release of LOST SOULS Issue 03! \n\n\
 n\nOur storytellers will share readings inspired by that centuries old co
 mmunity of practice\, the “coven”. Americo Alvarenga and C. H. Pearce 
 are to tell stories of benevolent authority and passive resistance\, and t
 he morbid curiosity in hearing voices of the dead. Megan Cook will reflect
  on everyday rituals of magic. Imogen Wall will recite poetry inspired by 
 how we make sense of magic. \n\n\n\nThe writers will be joined by singer a
 nd songwriter\, Maddie Jiang. She will perform songs inspired by darker\, 
 country-inspired folk music. \n\n\n\nOur night also aims to help honour th
 e Samhain (pronounced ‘sah-win’). Traditionally\, Samhain is celebrate
 d in late April or early May in the Southern Hemisphere (31st October in t
 he Northern Hemisphere). \n\n\n\nThis is the fifth event in the “Macabre
  Dreams” series hosted by Lost Souls Magazine.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T052100Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/spellbound-readings-and-music-lost-s
 ouls-macabre-dreams/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cut Worms (USA) with special guest John Andrews (USA)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260609T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260609T220000
DTSTAMP:20260414T123846
UID:ganggang-10001243-1781031600-1781042400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-17-at-11.30.21-am.png
CREATED:20260317T003144Z
DESCRIPTION:Transmitter is Max Clarke’s fourth full length record as C
 ut Worms\, due out March 13th via JagJaguwar. Produced by Jeff Tweedy at W
 ilco’s Loft studio\, Transmitter marks a deepening of Clarke’s abili
 ties and the convergence of two artists whose work searches for grace amid
  dislocation. Together\, they conjure the ecstatic spirits of power pop an
 d alt rock\, expanding Cut Worms’ vintage palette while reaffirming his 
 gift for timeless songwriting. \n\n\n\nWhile Clarke’s voice and writing 
 formed the framework\, Tweedy’s guitar and bass lines sketched the rooms
  the songs inhabit. Tweedy’s presence as a producer revealed itself not 
 in heavy-handed choices but in how he coloured spaces and continually offe
 red new textures. Between them\, their like-minded sensibilities bridged a
  generational gap to create something more nuanced than either might have 
 made alone. \n\n\n\nNow several albums into his career\, Clarke stands ful
 ly in command of his craft\, resonating at his own frequency. What began a
 s a passion for bygone pop has matured into a study of endurance itself\, 
 confirming him as a singer-songwriter of lasting depth. Transmitter finds 
 Clarke in full stride\, writing with the conviction of someone who’s mad
 e peace with uncertainty. These songs reckon with the cost of comfort and 
 return to the idea that beauty\, connection\, and love are not luxuries bu
 t necessities for survival. \n\n\n\nJohn Andrews has spent the past few ye
 ars tucked away in Red Hook\, Brooklyn – a neighborhood that sits just b
 eyond the natural drift of the city. Once shaped by maritime industry and 
 later a haven for artists in search of vast warehouse space\, its history 
 and isolation give it a quiet magnetism. Streetsweeper\, the fifth album
  by John Andrews & The Yawns\, reflects that vantage point-tranquil\, self
 -contained\, and curious about the movements most people overlook. \n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for al
 l. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We h
 ave zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to en
 sure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\,
  please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for eve
 ryone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri peopl
 e\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We
  pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and reco
 gnise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We ar
 e grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T003146Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/cut-worms-usa-with-special-guest-joh
 n-andrews-usa/
END:VEVENT
